# Atlas Master Reference deterministic projections and release bundles. These
# are exact-source derivatives, never authored source; each carries its own
# manifest and is regenerated from a clean tracked tree.
/master-reference/public/atlas-projection/
/master-reference/.atlas-compiler/
/master-reference/artifacts/
/master-reference/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# design-sync (claude.ai/design converter) — staged scripts, build output, machine state.
# The durable set (.design-sync/config.json, NOTES.md, conventions.md, previews/, docs/, overrides/) IS committed.
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
.design-sync/.cache/
.design-sync/learnings/
.design-sync/node_modules

# autonomous-brain: generated dated morning briefings (reproducible via /briefing).
# The command, hook, and scorecard schema ARE committed; the machine-generated output is not.
docs/briefings/briefing-*.md

# autonomous-brain: vault-digest recall store (ADR-0001 Amendment 1). The digest is DERIVED from the
# PERSONAL vault; even Rule-3-sanitized it is local-only by default (privacy-first) — the producer,
# consumer, gate, and format doc ARE committed; the digest data is not. Un-ignore deliberately if you
# decide a sanitized digest may live in the (pushable) repo.
docs/vault-digest/digest-*.jsonl

# The P2-0a real-query log — owner-machine only, like the vault digest above: a REAL query may name
# client tokens from another engagement (two-store rule, ADR 0001), so the data never enters the
# pushable repo. The writer (recall.log_query), schema doc, and tests ARE committed; the rows are not.
# (Human decision 2026-07-10, resolving the #319/#321 duplicate-design split.)
docs/quality/query_log.jsonl

# D10 retrieval-eval judge payload. The pairs file carries full corpus excerpts — INCLUDING
# vault-digest text — so it must never reach the pushable repo (two-store rule, ADR-0001).
# retrieval_eval.invoke_judge_helper now writes it to the system temp dir instead; this rule is the
# backstop for a leftover from a build that predates that (a hard kill skipped the cleanup `finally`).
docs/quality/.d10-judge-pairs.tmp.json
docs/quality/.d10-judge-pairs*.json

# Atlas portable build outputs (ADR-0004 P2) — the bundle is built, never committed
portable/build/
portable/dist/

# gate-ledger lock sidecars. Inert by design (they hold no data and are re-locked on the next run),
# and deliberately never unlinked: the sidecar IS the mutual-exclusion token, so removing one to tidy
# a directory can hand two writers the same lock on POSIX. See cisco_toolkit/gate_state.py ::
# _locked_update. Ignoring them is the right way to keep an engagement folder clean.
docs/engagement-state.json.lock
*.json.lock
